[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2603065457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101750#issuecomment-2603065457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101750","id":2603065457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bJ6Bx","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-20T18:47:01Z","updated_at":"2025-01-20T18:48:00Z","body":"I've tried playing around with the VisualInstance3D layers property (which determines what the GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D takes into account when generating its collision shape). However, all collisions still occur as soon as `layers` is not equal to `0`. If it's equal to `0`, then all collision is disabled.\n\nChanging `cull_mask` doesn't impact the collisions in any way (it's used to make different particles collide with different shapes instead; here, we want to exclude specific objects from the generated collision). Note that since `cull_mask` defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF` and only the first 20 layers are visible in the editor, you'll need to set `cull_mask = 0` in a `@tool` script to actually disable all layers (including the editor-specific layers that are otherwise hidden).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2603065457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608761450","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101750#issuecomment-2608761450","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101750","id":2608761450,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bfopq","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T03:18:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T03:18:21Z","body":"Also interesting to note is that this occurs with all nodes that inherit from Node3D and have an icon. \n\nHere it also collides with the icon of a AudioListener3D node.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca1cb227-190e-4468-86f8-307ab9cda26c)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608761450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614024648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101750#issuecomment-2614024648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101750","id":2614024648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bztnI","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T16:38:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T16:38:54Z","body":"For reference, this happens now because the alpha-scissor gizmos are written to the depth buffer. GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D works by having its own viewport from a top-down view and reads the depth buffer. This is why you see the gizmos in a fixed orientation in the particle collision: they are still billboarded, but they are facing the camera used for the depth buffer generation.\n\nAdding `icon->set_depth_draw_mode(StandardMaterial3D::DEPTH_DRAW_DISABLED);` to `EditorNode3DGizmoPlugin::create_icon_material()` fixes the issue, but it reintroduces the issues that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/91174 resolved (such as gizmos not appearing behind refractive materials anymore).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614024648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]